WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.887
The tooling is one script
with five commands.

2
00:00:02.887 --> 00:00:07.093
Lint applies twelve rules to any
definition, including Microsoft's,

3
00:00:07.093 --> 00:00:10.471
and one of them adds up every
possible retry wait so the

4
00:00:10.471 --> 00:00:13.775
callback can't arrive after
the workflow has given up.

5
00:00:13.775 --> 00:00:16.284
Run plays a definition against the fakes,

6
00:00:16.284 --> 00:00:19.163
with failures and repeat
deliveries on demand.

7
00:00:19.163 --> 00:00:22.400
Build refuses to write anything
while there's a finding.

8
00:00:22.400 --> 00:00:26.989
And the two checks compare what's
really in the tenant with the registry,

9
00:00:26.989 --> 00:00:29.089
including Book 03's leaver order:

10
00:00:29.089 --> 00:00:33.600
block the account and revoke its tokens
first, then run the custom task.

11
00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:36.890
A failed revocation shouldn't
stop the cleanup after it.
